# The relation disjoint of IEEE 1788 of two intervals with 2-limb bounds (milestone2.md,
# "Comparisons", the relations of IEEE 1788, and "IEEE 1788"): X and Y have no member in common. An
# empty operand is disjoint from everything; otherwise x_u < y_l or y_u < x_l. Exact. For every
# precision.
kernel:        interval_rel_disjoint_2
input:         xl = xl0 xl1
input:         xu = xu0 xu1
input:         yl = yl0 yl1
input:         yu = yu0 yu1
output:        mask m
requires:      interval xl xu
requires:      interval yl yu
ensures:       certain m disjoint x y x=xl,xu y=yl,yu exact
min_precision: 1
source:        the stored bounds compared, and tests of emptiness (Milestone 2 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeIntervalPredicates.v interval_rel_disjoint_2_correct
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the result is a mask, which has no non-finite value, and a comparison with NaN is false; certain states what comes out for every canonical operand

ex = eq(xl0, const inf)
ey = eq(yl0, const inf)
ee = or(ex, ey)
da = lt_2_2(xu0, xu1, yl0, yl1)
db = lt_2_2(yu0, yu1, xl0, xl1)
dd = or(da, db)
m  = or(ee, dd)
